//! task: write
//! ask: Declare a C function from the foreign library, with an explicit ABI.
//! expect: ok
//! refs: §5.3, §4.6
//! explain: `externus("C", abi: sysv_amd64) { ... }` opens a foreign block with an explicit ABI; the admitted ABIs are `sysv_amd64`, `aapcs64` and `lp64d`. A raw pointer `*T` requires `Crudum`, so the foreign signature declares it. Non-atomic `refero` may not cross the boundary (`EXS-E0520`).

externus("C", abi: sysv_amd64) {
    functio strlen(s: *u8) -> mensura poscit Crudum
}
